    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45952" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sublĭgācŭlum</span></b> ,
			i, n.
		subligo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a waistband</i>, <i>breech -
			cloth</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Off. 1, 35, 129</span></i>; cf.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 19, 21</span></i>.—Called
			subsequently <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sublĭ-gar</span></b> , āris,
			n., <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 87, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6,
			70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 12, 14, 32, § 59</span></i>; and
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sublĭgātūra</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i><span class="en">Theod.
				Prisc. 1, 26</span></i>.</div>
